{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>a forger of every cutting tool of copper and iron.</b> Its meaning is: he was a forger (לֹטֵשׁ) and a cutter/hewer (חוֹרֵשׁ) of all copper and iron. That is to say, he would sharpen and cut/hew every craft of copper and iron. Similar to it: כָּל תִּשָּׂא עָוֹן וְקַח טוֹב — 'forgive all iniquity and take the good' (Hosea 14:3). And according to the opinion of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 4:22), it is connected to the preceding verses: he was the father of one who forged every cutting tool of copper and iron." "<b>And the sister of Tuval-Cain was Na'amah.</b> That is, as if saying: and a sister was born to him, and her name was Na'amah. Similarly: וַאֲחוֹת לוֹטָן תִּמְנָע — 'and the sister of Lotan was Timna' (Genesis 36:22); וְאֵת מִרְיָם אֲחוֹתָם — 'and Miriam their sister' (Numbers 26:59); וְשֵׁם אֲחוֹתוֹ מַעֲכָה — 'and the name of his sister was Ma'akhah' (I Chronicles 7:15). And in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 23:3), some say she was the wife of Noah, and why did they call her Na'amah? Because her deeds were pleasing (נָאִים) and sweet (נְעִימִים). They intended to say that she had a name in those generations, for she was a righteous woman and gave birth to righteous ones, and therefore Scripture mentions her — and if so, a small remnant of Cain survived in the world. And if we say that she was not the woman from whom Noah begot his three sons, then there is no reason for Scripture to mention her. And another midrash from our Sages: she was the very beautiful woman through whom the sons of Elohim strayed, and she is the one hinted at in the verse וַיִּרְאוּ בְנֵי הָאֱלֹהִים אֶת בְּנוֹת הָאָדָם — 'and the sons of Elohim saw the daughters of men' (Genesis 6:2), as mentioned in Pirkei Rabbi Eliezer (22). And others said (Zohar Ḥadash 1:19b) that she was the wife of Shamdon, the mother of Ashmedai, and from her the demons were born — for thus her name is found in the writings of the practical use of demons. And Scripture alludes and is brief concerning mysteries such as these."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The Hosea 14:3 citation follows Ramban's Hebrew text (כל תשא) rather than the standard Masoretic text of Hosea 14:3 (כל תשא עון וקח טוב vs. standard כל תשא עון וקח לך חסד). The slight textual discrepancy reflects Ramban's citation from memory."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:56.364993870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}